```sas
ods pdf file="output.pdf" startswith=" Journal of SAS Specialists ";
ods journal;
proc print data=sashelp.cars;
  title "Table of Cars";
  run;
ods journal close;
ods pdf close;
```
This code will create a PDF file named "output.pdf" with a journal-style layout. The `ods journal` statement initializes the journal style, and the `ods pdf` statement specifies the output destination.

In the `ods journal` statement, you can also specify additional options to customize the journal format. For example, you can change the font, font size, and margins:
```sas
ods journal font="Times New Roman" size=12;
ods journal margins top=1in bottom=1in left=1in right=1in;
```
You can also use the `ods` statement to customize the appearance of specific elements, such as titles and footnotes. For example:
```sas
ods title font="Arial" size=18 style=bold;
ods footnote font="Arial" size=12 style=italic;
